p_free),\n    (\"asn1-tlv\", asn1_free),\n    (\"delimited-fields\", delim_free),\n)\n\n\ndef register_speculative():\n    \"\"\"Hand the keyless free-text decoders to lib.decode's joint free-line assignment as day=None (speculative)\n    entries: only for a blob that has more lines than any confirmed codec day and a free line the confirmed codecs\n    can't cover. Idempotent.\"\"\"\n    from lib import decode\n    confirmed = {n for n, d, _f in decode._FREE if d is not None}\n    for name, fn in SPECULATIVE_FREE:\n        if name not in confirmed:   # rot47 = GM-confirmed D15: keep its day so it isn't demoted to speculative\n            decode.register_free(name, None, fn)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    for f in sys.argv[1:]:\n        print(f, (infer_case(f) or (\"unidentified\",))[0])\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":155,"oldLines":6,"newStart":155,"newLines":9,"lines":["     # D24 \"String Theory\" (\"Count carefully. The comma knows where to stop.\"): one netstring per character, `1:c,`","     # concatenated, no separators (byte-exact on the Single, TT 6b420728 and 118/118 Mastery 39a9fb2c line 24)","     (24, \"netstring\", lambda s: \"\".join(f\"1:{c},\" for c in s), netstr_dec, False),","+    # D25 \"You Have a Point\": one Unicode code point per character, `U+XXXX` (uppercase hex, >= 4 digits), single","+    # spaces (byte-exact on the Single, TT and 123/123 Mastery 0b1ae1d0 line 25)","+    (25, \"uplus\", lambda s: \" \".join(f\"U+{ord(c):04X}\" for c in s), uplus_dec, False),"," ]"," "," try:   # fair runs (HCTF_CODEC_MAX_DAY=<N-1>, as lib/codec.py): only codecs GM-confirmed before day N"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lhc8RAEN2yLqewtFvfCpRe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
