{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BoNofa2ZTaZ6mwkrgWd7ek","type":"tool_result","content":"== binary-out-of-bounds\nNOTES.md\ncases\nsolve.py\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D15) the \"4.84 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6.6, harness cProfile counted 1.1 s of imports and 2.9 s of thread waits) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.90 s wall (critical path = AES-CTR+inflate of the 67 MB d08 member ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).\n\n## D17 (decoder-ring) single\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/vocab.json: storage / hcfg_storage = \"base64\" for a base64 (SENGR...) stored HCFG (GM D17 d09/d08/d11/d13); \"raw\" REJECTED for raw-stored (D17 d12/d14).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D17) the \"3.31 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5; harness cProfile counted ~1.1 s of imports and ~2.4 s of thread waits) -- isolated: solve.py 0.8-0.9 s wall on the 204-id single (run_solver 0.87 s; tottime is 0.24 s threaded zlib inflate of the AES members + ~0.2 s imports), 1.1 s inside the full concurrent solver-test; all 31 cases green. `hctf solver-run` wall (~6.5 s) is CLI/harness startup under load, not the solver. d12/d14 `hcfg_storage` (raw-stored) stay intentionally empty (unresolved GM label), so the single outputs 202/204.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D20) the \"5.28 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~10; the harness cProfile of the same case totals 2.2 s, mostly thread waits + imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.61 s wall unpinned, 0.61-0.74 s pinned to 1-2 CPUs on the 240-id single; in-process answer() work is 0.28 s CPU once members are decoded, unzip 0.55 s CPU (67 MB d08 inflate ~0.16 s, pycryptodome AES-CTR 25 MB ~0.1 s, sha256 ~0.04 s, all GIL-free threads); full suite passes, Mastery 0.6-2.6 s. d20_analysis_hcfg_resource_size = RS20 u32le @ magic+8 (380 on the single, matches expected).\n== mobile-integrity-signals\ncases\nsolve.py\n== scripting-ashes-to-assets\nNOTES.md\n__pycache__\nbashplan.py\nbatchplan.py\ncases\njsdecode.js\npowerplay.py\npyplan.py\nsolve.py\nvbsplan.py\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.codec` import is ~0.3 s, almost all of it from ~340 module-level `re.compile`s (cProfile, D24 single). Compiling lazily would save that on every script-lane solver start.\n- Solver skeleton: when `group_by_set` gives one group, split the questions by artifact across forked workers (independent members), like D24 solve.py `main()`.\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n- `lib.common._zip_open`: prefetch WinZip-AES keys for all members in parallel (salt = bytes after the local header; `hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac` in a ThreadPoolExecutor), as D23 solve.py `_prefetch_keys` does. Every script-lane Mastery solver pays ~1 ms x members serially today.\n- `lib.codec`: ~295 module-level `re.compile`s cost ~0.3 s per solver start, and `_find_codecs_uncached` runs ~16 regex probes per text (4669 searches / 287 texts = 0.4 s on the D23 Mastery). Compile lazily and gate each detector on a cheap substring test (`'Codec_' in text`, ...).\n== web-reset-expectations\n__pycache__\ncases\nsolve.py\n== web-resolver-revolt\n__pycache__\ncases\nsolve.py\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/solver/solve.py:2:\"\"\"Node by Node (Day 7): the Day 6 bundle plus inert Node.js .mjs operation graphs (lib.codec) and Bash\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/solver/solve.py:19:from lib import codec  # noqa: E402\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/solver/solve.py:377:def _codec_hint(data):\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/solver/solve.py:378:    \"\"\"First declared codec lib.codec decodes to a plan (no interpreter), or None.\"\"\"\nchallenges/day25/scripting-ashes-to-assets/solver/